(f) Award [2 max]
Referential integrity refers to relationships between tables in a database;
Referential integrity is maintained by the connection between the primary key in one table 
and
the foreign key in another;
Which ensures records are appropriately updated (e.g. FK value cannot be changed to a value
that does not exist as a PK);
It cascades updates and deletes from the PK table to the FK table;
To prevent update anomalies and orphan records;
